hor name / Procedia Computer Science  00 (2024) 000 –000 \n2.1. Cloud platform  \nHugging Face provides the server and software infrastructure to host t he interface. This means that participants \ncan access the chatbot over the internet from any PC or phone browser at a specified URL, or it may be embedded in \nanother application as an iFrame. The Hugging Face softw are infrastructure includes a Python development \nenvironment and Gradio user interface libraries. For transparency, the Python code is publicly viewable on Hugging \nFace  [30], but security features such as API private key management and secure areas maintain the privacy of API \nkeys and any course documents used.  \nThe chat function takes place in Open -AI’s gpt-3.5-turbo -0125  model via the API secured with project specific \naccount credentials. The Hugging Face interface concatenates the prompt, user messages and AI responses to pass to \nthe ChatGPT model over the secure
account credentials. The Hugging Face interface concatenates the prompt, user messages and AI responses to pass to \nthe ChatGPT model over the secure  API, and collects the response to display in the interface. The API is secured  \nInterface  \nHuggingface  \nChat GPT \n(Open AI)  \nLogging    \n(e.g. Airta ble)  \nChatGPT \nInterface \n(Prompt, \nHistory)  \nReporting    \n(e.g. Padlet)  \nMedica l \nDocuments  \nAPI \nAPI \nhttp \nFig. 1. Architecture of the system and sample output
